notes:
Searched on area2 x *measured* avg_ticks rather than the area2 x corridor_cells proxy every prior
sweep in this repo used. build_room costs 5-18s but optimize.verify on the fast engine costs
0.05-0.08s — under 1% of an evaluation — so the proxy was never necessary, and searching ticks
directly prices each lever with its row cost already counted.

Block visits, not glyphs, are the bill: gradebook ran 2,496 visits against 322 glyph cells and
15,510 grid ticks against an op model of 1,726 — 89% of ticks are corridor, ~39 a visit. Fusing
every two-visit loop (5 each) cut visits 32.7% (gradebook) and 19.5% (snake). corridor_cells rose
on both while ticks fell: static corridor is not what a case walks. Geometry was not spent either
— flat_relay (a two-row turnaround; relay's three rows are a property of the perimeter walk) gave
gradebook a row, and snake's north band folded 12 rows to 6, which bought four columns since
snake's charged side was its width.

Previous: 155,285,258. 

Supersedes 109,180,919: that commit pinned a stale read of a still-running search's output file
(the 46s improvement at 12,773 rather than the order the run finished on at 178s, 12,695). Same
geometry, better block order. gradebook's pin was re-checked the same way and matches its result
file exactly, so only snake was affected. Read a search's result file after the process is dead,
and diff the pin against the file rather than against whichever log line was visible.
